WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.550
The Jedi Order, Rebels tie-ins, and an ominously
familiar Sith.

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:06.410
The first trailer for "Obi-Wan Kenobi" is
here.

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:09.059
Did you catch these little details?

00:00:09.059 --> 00:00:13.050
If you know why Obi-Wan is on Tatooine, you
might've expected this detail, but it is nonetheless

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:17.390
cool to see: in the teaser, we get a glimpse
of Obi-Wan observing Uncle Owen and Aunt Beru

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:21.099
from some high ground, and sure enough, the
Jedi's binoculars settle on what appears to

00:00:21.099 --> 00:00:23.199
be a young Luke Skywalker pretending to pod-race.

00:00:23.199 --> 00:00:27.820
As Star Wars fans know very well, Obi-Wan's
task is to protect him at all cost, and this

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:31.619
appearance of Luke certainly gives us a lot
of information as to how many years have passed

00:00:31.619 --> 00:00:33.360
since the events of "Revenge of the Sith."

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.640
Based on what we can see, Luke seems to be
about 10 years old.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.170
This means that the events of "Obi-Wan Kenobi"
will likely be picking up not too long after

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:41.170
"Revenge of the Sith."

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:44.710
It will be interesting to see how Obi-Wan
manages his duty of protecting Luke while

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.180
remaining out of sight.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:49.809
Either way, "Obi-Wan Kenobi" promises to bring
greater insight into the young Luke's life

00:00:49.809 --> 00:00:53.000
on Tatooine, even if Luke himself only features
briefly.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.840
In the new teaser trailer, perhaps one of
the first things that strikes fans of "Star

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.350
Wars" is the ominous and immediately recognizable
soundtrack.

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:03.550
This is, of course, the John Williams masterpiece
from "Star Wars: The Phantom Menace," called

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:04.550
"Duel of the Fates."

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:08.400
"Duel of the Fates" was previously used during
the epic confrontation between Obi-Wan, Qui-Gon

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.830
Jinn, and Darth Maul in the first movie of
the prequel trilogy.

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:15.830
Its usage in the "Obi-Wan" trailer pays tribute
to this earlier struggle, but at this point,

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:19.340
it seems that the point is to more squarely
focus on the past and future of Obi-Wan as

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:22.970
he struggles to find his fate in a galaxy
that seeks his death.

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:26.760
It seems like the "Obi-Wan Kenobi" series
is gunning for more than your everyday tie-ins

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:30.760
to the films, because the new trailer also
shows off several of the infamous Inquisitors.

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:34.611
The Inquisitors, for those who missed out
on the TV series "Star Wars Rebels," are a

00:01:34.611 --> 00:01:38.550
group of force-sensitives enlisted by the
Empire to hunt down the remaining Jedi.

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:42.290
Personally trained by Darth Vader, and often
former Jedi themselves, the Inquisitors play

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:46.140
a large part in further eradicating the Jedi
in the years following Order 66.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:49.850
Throughout the trailer, we are shown three
different Inquisitors, two of which have appeared

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:51.570
in previous "Star Wars" stories.

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:55.710
The first of these is the Grand Inquisitor,
an ex-Jedi Pau'an with white skin and distinctive

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:56.710
face markings.

00:01:56.710 --> 00:02:00.280
He plays an important role as a primary villain
throughout much of "Rebels," as well as in

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:01.520
several comics.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:05.181
The other known Inquisitor is the Fifth Brother,
who was also a common sight in "Rebels" as

00:02:05.181 --> 00:02:06.470
a minor villain.

00:02:06.470 --> 00:02:10.509
The only Inquisitor we don't know much about
is Reva, played by Moses Ingram, who we see

00:02:10.509 --> 00:02:14.000
getting involved in a number of tense confrontations
throughout the trailer.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.750
Based on this, it's clear that the Inquisitors
are set to play a major role as antagonists

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:21.610
throughout the series, potentially crossing
sabers with Obi-Wan ... though, given that

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:25.310
Obi-Wan manages to make it to "A New Hope"
alive, that may not go half as well as they

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:26.310
think.

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:30.270
The universe of "Star Wars" is filled with
strange and amazing animals, and some humanoids

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:34.900
that straddle the line between person and
animal – looking at you, Chewie.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:35.920
"Luke?

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:36.920
Luke's crazy!"

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:40.440
Obi-Wan himself is no stranger to hanging
out with a menagerie of space beasts, having

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:43.450
ridden everything from varactyls to aiwha
over the years.

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:46.630
In the "Obi-Wan" trailer, the character is
shown riding something that appears to be

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:47.630
a camel.

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:51.080
This might strike the casual "Star Wars" fan
off-guard — after all, there's no way a

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:53.550
Star Wars show would put a camel on Tatooine.

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:54.920
"No camels."

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:56.870
Han Solo's right: it isn't a camel.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:59.690
It's actually a four-legged herbivore known
as an "eopie."

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:03.360
Originally from Tatooine, their adaptations
to the harsh environment make them very useful

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:07.090
for carrying luggage or people across the
desert ... you know, just like the camels

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:08.590
in our world.

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:10.660
The nostalgia is strong with this one.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:14.390
At one point during the new "Obi-Wan" trailer,
fans are greeted by the return appearance

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:18.490
of actor Joel Edgerton's Uncle Owen character,
who many "Star Wars" fans will remember served

00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:22.840
as Anakin Skywalker's step-brother in "Episode
II – Attack of the Clones" and Luke Skywalker's

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:26.210
guardian on Tatooine at the end of "Revenge
of the Sith."

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:28.030
Not surprisingly, fans are psyched.

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:32.230
In the "Obi-Wan" trailer, the show's big new
bad — Reva the Inquisitor — comes face-to-face

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:36.459
with Edgerton's Owen after arriving on Tatooine
with her evil Empire cronies.

00:03:36.459 --> 00:03:40.180
Actor Bonnie Piesse, who played Uncle Owen's
girlfriend in Episodes II and III, is also

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:42.300
set to appear as her Aunt Beru character.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:46.140
As fans know, the two characters are fated
to be tragically killed off in "A New Hope"

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:49.730
by Imperial Stormtroopers, but this will mark
the first time we truly see what their life

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:52.210
while raising the future Jedi hero was like.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:55.920
While the "Obi-Wan Kenobi" teaser trailer
was packed to the brim with references and

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.730
epic glimpses of things to come, there's one
little moment that appears so briefly that

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:02.180
only die-hard fans would notice it on the
first watch.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:06.340
At one point, an unknown hand touches what
appears to be a symbol carved into a wall,

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:10.410
which appears to be the official Jedi Order
crest: a lightsaber with elaborate wings on

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:11.530
either side.

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:15.600
It's crudely carved, but it’s an important
symbol for the Jedi Order, serving as an official

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:19.190
insignia for them for thousands of years before
their eventual fall.

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:22.610
It being carved into the wall like graffiti
is an indicator, perhaps, that hope for the

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:24.470
return of the Jedi remains strong.

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:28.220
That said, because this moment is so brief,
there's no definitive evidence that this is

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:31.600
the crest of the Jedi Order, and it could
be something else entirely.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:35.900
While Darth Vader doesn't physically appear
in the "Obi Wan Kenobi" limited series teaser

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:37.840
trailer, his presence looms large.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:41.940
And fans who listen carefully can hear Vader's
iconic breathing at the very end of the teaser

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:42.940
trailer.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:46.320
Hayden Christensen, who played Anakin Skywalker
in "Attack of the Clones" and "Revenge of

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:51.150
the Sith," was confirmed to co-star as Darth
Vader in the upcoming series back in 2020.

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:54.669
Lucasfilm president Kathleen Kennedy promised
Christensen's return to "Star Wars" would

00:04:54.669 --> 00:04:58.030
result in "the rematch of the century" between
Vader and Kenobi.

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:01.389
Given the heavy presence within the trailer
of the Empire's Inquisitors, it's probably

00:05:01.389 --> 00:05:04.770
safe to say Vader will oversee their efforts
to find Kenobi.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:09.030
In October 2021, The Hollywood Reporter also
reported that the now 40-year-old actor will

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:13.230
also reprise his role as Darth Vader in the
upcoming series "Ahsoka," alongside Rosario

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:14.230
Dawson.

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:19.010
Ahsoka Tano and Anakin Skywalker grew close
as Jedi padawan and master through "Star Wars:

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:23.350
The Clone Wars," making the upcoming series
a second long-awaited reunion between fan

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:24.350
favorites.

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:28.550
As for what role Vader plays in the future
of Obi-Wan Kenobi, that still remains to be

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:29.550
seen.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:30.550
Well, sort of.

